//- Early Access, stated plainly.
//-
//- Meta's own Early Access guidance asks for this on the listing, and the same
//- reasoning applies to the page that sends people there: a buyer who knows
//- what they are getting writes a two-star review about the thing that annoyed
//- them, and a buyer who was surprised writes a one-star review about the
//- label. Every claim here is a fact that is true on launch day — nothing
//- about future pricing, and nothing promised on a date.
mixin earlyaccess(links, product)
  section#early-access.ea(data-screen-label="What Early Access means")
    .ea__inner
      .section-head
        .ornament
          span.rule
          span.diamond
          span.rule
        h2.h2 What Early Access means here
        p.serif-italic The expedition is real and playable. It is also still being extended.
      .ea-grid
        .ea-card
          span.ea-card__label In the game today
          ul.ea-card__list
            li Five destinations, each drawn from a real place where real treasure was found.
            li The whole loop — detector, pickaxe, pan, sieve, magnet and brush.
            li English and French, seated or standing, teleport or free movement.
            li No internet connection needed once it is installed.
        .ea-card
          span.ea-card__label What comes next
          ul.ea-card__list
            li Kimberley, the Western Australian diamond country, is built and waiting — it is the first destination to arrive after launch.
            li More sites after it, working toward twelve in the full version.
            li Six languages, translated by people rather than by machine.
        .ea-card
          span.ea-card__label How to push it along
          ul.ea-card__list
            li There is a feedback screen inside the game. It reaches the developer directly, and it does not ask who you are.
            li The camp gathers on Discord — that is where new destinations get argued about first.
          a.ea-card__link(href=links.discord target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Join the Discord
      p.ea__note
        | Built by one person in Victoria, Australia. If something is broken or
        | wrong — particularly if you actually swing a coil — that is worth
        | hearing about far more than a kind review.
